e reason cannot explain the preference unless the rule is interpreted differently. But strictly applying the rule as stated (probabilities strictly greater than 1/n), no outcome qualifies as probable in either lottery, making the reason inapplicable. Thus, the decision reason cannot be applied to this decision problem as defined.",
